        "original_id": "bf93e6ae-8c39-56d4-8d20-43b7b5b1f291",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"What's It Gonna Be\", \"Love Shy (Thinking About You)\", Escape from the Sun\n- People: Selim Ben Rabha, Simon McDevitt, Aaron Evers, Mina Poli, Michelle McKenna\n- Groups: H \"Two\" O, Platnum\n- Concepts: bassline, UK garage\n- Places: Sheffield, UK\n- Companies: Marrakesh Records\n\nFacts:\n- Bassline, also called bassline house, Niche, or 4x4, is a music genre related to UK garage that originated in Sheffield in the early 2000s.\n- \"What's It Gonna Be\" is a bassline song performed by H \"Two\" O and the British three-person bassline vocal group Platnum.\n- H \"Two\" O consists of Selim Ben Rabha, also known as \"Solution,\" and Simon McDevitt, also known as \"Oz,\" and they also go by \"Hit 'Em\" and \"Hard.\"\n- Platnum consists of Aaron Evers, Mina Poli, and Michelle McKenna.\n- \"Love Shy (Thinking About You)\" was released after the success of \"What's It Gonna Be\" with H \"Two\" O.\n- Escape from the Sun was released in April 2009 through Marrakesh Records and was available to buy in certain stores around the UK.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a64a5666-013b-5dcd-b4d7-b16d8bdcdfbb",
        "text": "Page: What's It Gonna Be (H &quot;Two&quot; O song). Sentence: is a bassline (subgenre of UK garage) song performed by the duo known as H \"Two\" O (Selim Ben Rabha, \"Solution\", and Simon McDevitt, \"Oz\", who also go by \"Hit 'Em\" and \"Hard\") and the British three-person bassline vocal group Platnum (Aaron Evers, Mina Poli, and Michelle McKenna).\nPage: Bassline (music genre). Sentence: Bassline (sometimes referred to as bassline house, Niche or 4x4) is a type of music related to UK garage that originated in Sheffield in the early 2000s.\nPage: Love Shy (Thinking About You). Sentence: It was released after the success of \"What's It Gonna Be\" with H \"Two\" O.\nPage: Escape from the Sun. Sentence: It was released in April 2009 through Marrakesh Records, available to buy in certain stores around the UK.",
